 ],
 "literal": "The king's request for alliance not giving, he who has prominent tusk / beautiful flower garland and adorned leaf-dress on her waist, / the father of the young woman with red-spotted anklets, / having inserted the wooden crossbar in the firm doorframe of the door, / where the fresh banners wave on the fortress wall, / ... / with fierce-eyed kinsmen like a pack of tigers, / not yielding to words, with wrathful anger, / saying 'gather flowers' and having commanded, entered the pond. / Tomorrow, with her, the gentle woman of unyielding nature adorned with shining jewels, / and beautiful breasts adorned with beauty spots, / either the day of entering marriage will happen, / or, with the body that resisted the long leaf-shaped spears, having churned the difficult battle with valor-rising strength, / entering the non-returning world is the other option, saying, / the chief took up his weapon. Meanwhile, / like a cool pond muddied by fighting elephants, / will it lose its great beauty, / this cool wetland town of gentle water settlement?",
 "translation": "The father of the young woman with red-spotted anklets, who wears a beautiful flower garland and an adorned leaf-dress on her waist, refuses to grant the king's request for alliance. He has barred his strong doors with heavy wooden crossbars, on whose fortress walls fresh banners wave. With his fierce-eyed kinsmen who are like a pack of tigers, he remains unyielding and wrathful. He has commanded his daughter to gather flowers and has entered the pond.\nThe chief of the attacking army, taking up his weapon, says: 'Either tomorrow will be the day of my marriage with that gentle, unyielding woman who is adorned with shining jewels and beauty spots on her lovely breasts, or I shall enter the world of no return, my body scarred by long, leaf-shaped spears after churning the fierce battle with rising valor and strength.'\nMeanwhile, like a cool pond muddied by fighting elephants, will this cool, fertile wetland town of gentle waters lose its great beauty?",
 "modern": "அரசர்களின் பெண் கேட்கும் வேண்டுகோளை ஏற்க மறுக்கும் தந்தை, தன் கோட்டைக் கதவுகளில் பெரிய மரத்தாழ்ப்பாள்களைப் போட்டுப் பூட்டியுள்ளான். அவனது கோட்டை மதில்களில் புதிய கொடிகள் அசைந்தாடுகின்றன. புலிக்குட்டம் போன்ற கொடிய சுற்றத்தாருடன் அவன் சினத்தோடு இருக்கிறான். தன் மகளைப் பூப்பறிக்க ஏவிவிட்டு அவன் குளத்திற்குள் இறங்கியுள்ளான். அவளை அடைய விரும்பும் தலைவன் தன் ஆயுதத்தைக் கையில் ஏந்தி, \"நாளை அந்த அணிகலன்கள் அணிந்த மெல்லியலாளோடு எனக்குத் திருமணம் நடக்க வேண்டும்; அல்லது, போர்க்களத்தில் பகைவரின் நீண்ட வேல்களால் என் உடல் துளைக்கப்பட்டு நான் வீரசுவர்க்கம் புக வேண்டும்\" என்று சபதம் செய்கிறான். யானைகள் சண்டையிடுவதால் கலங்கிப்போகும் குளிர்ந்த குளத்தைப் போல, மென்மையான நீர் வளம் கொண்ட இந்த மருத நிலத்து ஊர் தன் அழகையெல்லாம் இழந்து அழியப் போகிறதோ?",
 "explanation": "This poem belongs to the Kañci tiṇai and the theme of Makaṭpāṟ Kāñci (the tragedy of a daughter's beauty). A local chief refuses to give his beautiful daughter in marriage to the great kings who demand her hand. The girl's father prepares for war, locking his fortress gates and gathering his fierce, tiger-like kinsmen. Meanwhile, the suitor chief takes up his weapons, declaring that tomorrow he will either marry the girl or die heroically on the battlefield. The poet laments that this beautiful, fertile wetland town, currently rich with gentle waters, will soon be devastated by war, comparing its impending ruin to a peaceful pond muddied and ruined by fighting elephants.",
